I read an article about how celebrities deal with criticism, where Priyanka Chopra spoke about the importance of self-validation. She mentioned that people often give unnecessary importance and privileges to 
celebrities, which can deeply influence their personal lives. This constant attention can change how they think — what they should or shouldn’t do — and sometimes force them to live under pressure or in certain 
circumstances. Priyanka emphasized that every individual, including celebrities, should have the freedom to make their own choices and live life on their own terms.

She also added that celebrities are often affected by online trolls, which can become a major barrier in their journey. To overcome this, she suggested that instead of paying attention to negativity, one should 
surround themselves with a close circle of friends or family who can give honest and supportive feedback. This helps them grow and maintain a positive mindset.

At the end of the day, Priyanka concluded that you must live your life your own way. No one else should have the power to influence your choices — your path belongs to you alone.
